      "source_sentence": "8, P(TMPMT-co-Th)/PEDOT could be repeatedly switched up to 500 cycles retaining most (85%) of its electroactivity.",
      "evidence_id": "ev017"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_2_34",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        68.0,
        762.0,
        485.0,
        925.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "For the spectroelectrochemical studies, P(TMPMT-co-PTh) was synthesized in the presence of 40 mg TMPMT, $1 . 2 \\times \\mathrm { \\dot { 1 } 0 } ^ { - 3 } \\mathrm { M }$thiophene, 0.1 M TBAFB/ borontrifloride ethylether (BFEE) (8:2, v/v) in AN at 1.5 V, in a UV-cuvette equipped with ITO working and Pt counter electrodes with $\\mathbf { A } \\mathbf { g } /$${ \\bf A } { \\bf g } ^ { + }$reference electrode via constant potential electrolysis.",
      "evidence_id": "ev018"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_4_55",
      "page": 4,
      "bbox": [
        68.0,
        524.0,
        485.0,
        623.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "The solution side of film was significantly diferent than that of pristine polythiophene (Fig. 3(b)) which might be considered as a further proof of copolymerization.",
      "evidence_id": "ev019"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_2_37",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        518.0,
        633.0,
        937.0,
        925.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "0.01 M solution of EDOT in 0.1 M $\\mathrm { T B A B F _ { 4 } / A N }$was used to deposit the PEDOT film onto ITO electrode at $+ 1 . 5 \\mathrm { V ~ v s . ~ A g / A g ^ { + } }$.",
      "evidence_id": "ev020"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_0_6",
      "page": 0,
      "bbox": [
        69.0,
        471.0,
        935.0,
        694.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "Electrochemical copolymerization of TMPMT with thiophene in acetonitrile/boron trifluoride diethyl etherate (AN/BFEE) solvent mixture was achieved using tetrabutylammonium tetrafluoroborate (TBAFB) as the supporting electrolyte.",
      "evidence_id": "ev021"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_0_6",
      "page": 0,
      "bbox": [
        69.0,
        471.0,
        935.0,
        694.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "Resulting copolymer was characterized via cyclic voltammetry (CV), Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy (FTIR), scanning electron microscopy (SEM), four probe technique conductivity measurement and UV–Vis spectroscopy.",
      "evidence_id": "ev022"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_1_25",
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": [
        60.0,
        890.0,
        477.0,
        925.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "The IR spectrum was recorded on a Nicolet 510 FTIR spectrometer, where samples were dispersed in KBr.",
      "evidence_id": "ev023"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_1_25",
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": [
        60.0,
        890.0,
        477.0,
        925.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "Scanning electron microscopy (SEM) studies were performed by JEOL JSM-6400.",
      "evidence_id": "ev024"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_4_55",
      "page": 4,
      "bbox": [
        68.0,
        524.0,
        485.0,
        623.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "SEM micrograph of solution side of P(TMPMTco-Th) film showed homogenous compact structures in granular form (Fig. 3(a)).",
      "evidence_id": "ev025"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_1_25",
